Subject: [PATCH] usb: core: check fast-enum port status 1ms after reset
Upstream-Status: Pending

The DWC2 root-hub SetPortFeature(RESET) implementation holds reset for 50ms
and clears it synchronously before returning.  Waiting another 60ms before
the first status read delays discovery of a port-enable interrupt which has
already fired.

For USB_PORT_QUIRK_FAST_ENUM ports, reading status 1ms after the synchronous
reset operation avoids that idle wait.  Failed resets still use the normal
HUB_LONG_RESET_TIME delay before retrying.  Devices already known to be low
speed retain their conservative first status-check delay.

---
 drivers/usb/core/hub.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)
--- a/drivers/usb/core/hub.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/core/hub.c
@@ -2913,6 +2913,7 @@ static enum usb_device_speed port_speed(struct usb_hub *hub, u16 portstatus)
 #define DETECT_DISCONNECT_TRIES 5
 
 #define HUB_ROOT_RESET_TIME	60	/* times are in msec */
+#define HUB_FAST_RESET_TIME	1
 #define HUB_SHORT_RESET_TIME	10
 #define HUB_BH_RESET_TIME	50
 #define HUB_LONG_RESET_TIME	200
@@ -4956,6 +4957,8 @@ hub_port_init(struct usb_hub *hub, struct usb_device *udev, int port1,
 	/*  be a bit pessimistic with those devices. RHbug #23670 */
 	if (oldspeed == USB_SPEED_LOW)
 		delay = HUB_LONG_RESET_TIME;
+	else if (port_dev->quirks & USB_PORT_QUIRK_FAST_ENUM)
+		delay = HUB_FAST_RESET_TIME;
 
 	/* Reset the device; full speed may morph to high speed */
 	/* FIXME a USB 2.0 device may morph into SuperSpeed on reset. */
-- 
